{
 "author_name": "HeavyMap",
 "author_url": "https://heavymap.com/journey",
 "content": [
  {
   "children": [
    "working-paper, routine, method"
   ],
   "tag": "aside"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "A working paper written on 2026-10-18, published nearly as written. Local file paths, private repository names and personal names have been removed."
   ],
   "tag": "blockquote"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Status:"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " DRAFT, living doc. Proposed by an agent 2026-10-03 for the owner's review. Not yet owned by a Linear issue (",
    {
     "children": [
      "owner_issue"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " is ",
    {
     "children": [
      "proposed"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " in the planning index). Modelled on the ",
    {
     "children": [
      "na-research"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " Sector Research routine: slice the work, record every fact with its source, gate each step, and keep review decisions with the owner."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "HeavyMap has a large source catalog and a small number of datasets that anyone has actually opened. This routine turns catalog rows into profiled, harmonized, join-tested layers, one slice at a time. It is built on the EPIC-02 pilot (",
    {
     "children": [
      "EPIC-02-spine-and-joins.md"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "), which showed that the useful facts are small and checkable: record count, id field and its quirks, encoding, CRS, and how the layer joins to the parcel spine. Agents do the reading and write it down. the owner decides what is used and what is shown."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "For write-ups at the verify stage, model them on the NA-79 evidence docs: ",
    {
     "children": [
      "docs/normalization/ny-sbl-sources.md"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " and ",
    {
     "children": [
      "docs/normalization/ny-sbl-real-data-evidence.md"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " (on PR #56)."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "1.-Purpose-and-rules"
   },
   "children": [
    "1. Purpose and rules"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Purpose"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Detail: Produce, per layer: a profile, a quirks log, a harmonization result, a spine-join grade, and a use decision."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Pull needs no licence confirmation"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Detail: Pulling is for profiling only. Licence and use are decided later (",
      {
       "children": [
        "not_used"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " or a use decision)."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Pulled data stays local"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Detail: Raw pulls live in git-ignored local data (not published), never in git."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Owner and personal fields"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Detail: Pulled with everything else (",
      {
       "children": [
        "outFields=*"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ") and kept local. Screened out of anything public (tiles, site files, UI, exports) at the publish boundary, per D-13 and HARD-RULES 2. Record field names only, never values, in sheets, docs, PRs and comments."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "MPAC"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Detail: May be pulled, used and published. In Ontario, roll numbers, tax or property class and parcel civic addresses may be shown publicly (HARD-RULES 4)."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "NPCA-derived layers"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Detail: May be pulled, used and published, all fields pulled, identifying fields screened from public view (HARD-RULES 2, 5)."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Publication"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Detail: Public publish still needs the owner's per-jurisdiction beta-gate sign-off (NA-269). Publish/deploy tooling may be built and tested (HARD-RULES 3)."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Repo hygiene"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Detail: Docs and CSVs only on a branch and PR. No MCS edits, no secrets, no UK datasets."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
